{
  "title": "How to filter a list with LINQ?",
  "content": "I have a list of numbers and wat to keep only the even ones. What is the idiomatic way?",
  "tags": ["linq", "c#"]
}

###

GET {{StackOverflowClone_HostAddress}}/api/questions/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### Cała lista
GET {{StackOverflowClone_HostAddress}}/api/questions

### Strona 1, po 2 pytania
GET {{StackOverflowClone_HostAddress}}/api/questions?pageSize=2

### Strona 2, po 2 pytania
GET {{StackOverflowClone_HostAddress}}/api/questions?pageSize=2&page=2

### Filtr: c#
GET {{StackOverflowClone_HostAddress}}/api/questions?tag=c%23

### Filtr: docker
GET {{StackOverflowClone_HostAddress}}/api/questions?tag=docker

### Filtr: nieistniejący tag
GET {{StackOverflowClone_HostAddress}}/api/questions?tag=nieistniejacy

### Błąd: page=0
GET {{StackOverflowClone_HostAddress}}/api/questions?page=0

### Błąd: pageSize=100
GET {{StackOverflowClone_HostAddress}}/api/questions?pageSize=100

### Błąd: sort=7
GET {{StackOverflowClone_HostAddress}}/api/questions?sort=7

### Błąd: sort=abc
GET {{StackOverflowClone_HostAddress}}/api/questions?sort=abc
